$$<p>The Department of School Education, Government of Telangana, has released the notification for the Telangana Teacher Eligibility Test (TG TET) January 2027. The notification, Rc.No. 555/TGTET-January-2027/2026, was issued on 13 November 2026. Online applications open on Monday 16 November 2026 and close on 10 December 2026, and the computer-based examination will run from 3 to 15 January 2027.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><td>Examination</td><td>Telangana Teacher Eligibility Test (TG TET), January 2027</td></tr>
<tr><td>Conducted by</td><td>Department of School Education, Government of Telangana</td></tr>
<tr><td>Notification</td><td>13 November 2026, Rc.No. 555/TGTET-January-2027/2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Applications</td><td>16 November to 10 December 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Examination</td><td>3 to 15 January 2027 (computer-based test)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fee</td><td>Rs 750 for one paper, Rs 1,000 for both (General/BC); Rs 700 and Rs 950 (SC/ST/PwD)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hall tickets</td><td>From 28 December 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Results</td><td>8 to 12 February 2027</td></tr>
<tr><td>Apply at</td><td>tgtet.aptonline.in</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>What the test is</h2>
<p>TG TET is an eligibility test for teaching Classes I to VIII in Telangana. It is not a vacancy, so there is no post count to headline — passing the test makes a candidate eligible to apply for teaching posts when they are advertised. Paper I is for teaching Classes I to V, and Paper II is for teaching Classes VI to VIII. Candidates can appear for either paper or for both.</p>
<p>The examination is a computer-based test, held between 3 and 15 January 2027. Hall tickets will be available from 28 December 2026 through the official website of the school education department, and results are expected between 8 and 12 February 2027. Qualifying the test does not guarantee a teaching appointment — that depends on later recruitment by the state.</p>
<h2>Who can apply</h2>
<p>Candidates need a D.El.Ed or B.Ed to sit the test. The exact qualification combinations, category-wise relaxations and eligibility conditions must be confirmed from the detailed information bulletin, which is released on 16 November 2026. The bulletin, and the detailed notification, will be available from the same date on the official portals, so candidates should read those before applying rather than relying on summaries.</p>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<p>Apply and pay the fee online at tgtet.aptonline.in between 16 November and 10 December 2026. The fee depends on the category and on whether the candidate takes one paper or both. General and BC candidates pay Rs 750 for one paper and Rs 1,000 for both papers. SC, ST and PwD candidates pay Rs 700 for one paper and Rs 950 for both. The payment window stays open for the same dates as the application window, and both close on 10 December 2026.</p>
<h2>What the notification does not say</h2>
<p>The short notification does not carry the full eligibility rules. The detailed information bulletin, out on 16 November, is the document that settles the exact qualification combinations and relaxations, so any detail on eligibility should be checked against it. The subject-wise examination schedule will also be announced later, and the department has not published a separate vacancy figure because this is an eligibility test, not a recruitment of a fixed number of posts.</p>
<p>Never pay anyone who promises you a teaching post through TG TET. The test only certifies eligibility, and no agent or middleman can secure an appointment for you. Anyone asking for money in exchange for a pass or a posting should be treated as a scam. Apply only through the official portal, tgtet.aptonline.in.</p>
<p>Read also: <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/tntet-working-teachers-2026-20261027">TNTET 2026 — our report on the teacher eligibility test for working teachers</a>.</p>
<p>Sources: TG TET January 2027 notification, Rc.No. 555/TGTET-January-2027/2026, read through <a href="https://testbook.com/news/ts-tet-notification-2026-2027-out/">Testbook</a>, <a href="https://www.infusionnotes.com/tg-tet-notification-2027/">Infusion Notes</a>, <a href="https://www.schools360.in/tstet/">Schools360</a> and <a href="https://www.deccanchronicle.com/southern-states/telangana/tgtet-to-be-held-from-jan-3-to-15-2027-applications-open-from-nov-16-2004237">Deccan Chronicle</a>, and the official portal <a href="https://tgtet.aptonline.in/">tgtet.aptonline.in</a>.</p>$$,
$$<p>तेलंगाना सरकारको विद्यालय शिक्षा विभागले तेलंगाना शिक्षक योग्यता परीक्षा (TG TET) जनवरी २०२७ को सूचना जारी गरेको छ। सूचना Rc.No. 555/TGTET-January-2027/2026, १३ नोभेम्बर २०२६ मा जारी भएको हो। अनलाइन आवेदन सोमबार १६ नोभेम्बर २०२६ देखि खुल्छ र १० डिसेम्बर २०२६ सम्म दिन सकिन्छ, र कम्प्युटरमा आधारित परीक्षा ३ देखि १५ जनवरी २०२७ सम्म हुनेछ।</p>
